course: dictionary
lesson: 4072
title: Geordie: a person, a voice, a name
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: Geordie has three meanings, so look at the words around it to choose the right one. A Geordie is a person from Newcastle upon Tyne or Tyneside in North-East England. Geordie can also mean the strong local accent and dialect spoken there. Geordie is also a Scottish and Northern pet form of the name George.
explain: A dialect is a local way of speaking. It is not wrong English, it is just a different way of talking. «I'll walk fast, pet,» Nana says, and pet is a Geordie word for love or dear. Standard English is used in exams and formal writing, so you switch to it there.
explain: Read the clues. «A proud Geordie» is talking about a person. «They're soon talking pure Geordie» is talking about the way people speak. If you swap in the meaning and the sentence still makes sense, you have chosen well.
fact: A Geordie is a person from Newcastle upon Tyne or Tyneside in North-East England.
fact: Geordie is the strong local accent and dialect spoken in that area.
fact: «Howay» means come on, and «gan» means go.
fact: «Bairn» means child, «canny» means nice or good, and «nowt» means nothing.
fact: «Whey aye» means yes, of course. Dialect is not wrong English; Standard English is used for exams and formal writing.
exercise: «Howay, I'm fine man, let's gan» says Freya. What does howay mean? | Goodbye | Sorry | Be quiet | *Come on
exercise: What is a dialect? | A type of football kit | *A local way of speaking | A kind of maths sum | Wrong English that nobody should use
exercise: «They're soon talking pure Geordie.» What does Geordie mean here? | A football team | A pet name for George | A person from Newcastle | *The strong local accent and dialect
test: «I'll walk fast, pet,» Nana says. What does pet mean here? | Slowly | *Dear, a word showing love | A small animal | Tired
test: Which is a Scottish and Northern pet form of the name George? | Gordon | Gerald | Geoffrey | *Geordie
exam: In «a proud Geordie», what does Geordie mean? | A type of tree | A wet, grey day | A kind of sum | *A person from Newcastle
